{
  "id": "ep047",
  "duration": 48.816,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.089,
      "text": "Half of the Moon is permanently frozen in total darkness, right?",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Tsiolkovskiy crater Apollo 15.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tsiolkovskiy_crater_Apollo_15.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.089,
      "end": 9.209,
      "text": "Pop culture calls it the dark side, but that term originally meant unexplored.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "AS08-13-2319 - Apollo 8 - Apollo 8 Mission image, Target of Opportunity (T-O) 10 - NARA - 16670146.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown authorUnknown author or not provided",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AS08-13-2319_-_Apollo_8_-_Apollo_8_Mission_image,_Target_of_Opportunity_(T-O)_10_-_NARA_-_16670146.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.1,
          "end": 7.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 7.067,
          "end": 9.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9.209,
      "end": 16.154,
      "text": "In October 1959, the Soviet Luna 3 probe took the first photographs of this unseen face.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Luna 3 moon.jpg",
        "credit": "OKB-1",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luna_3_moon.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 9.2,
          "end": 16.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 16.154,
      "end": 23.374,
      "text": "Operating spacecraft on the far side requires relay satellites because the Moon blocks radio signals.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "QueqiaoDFH.jpg",
        "credit": "Zhang Lihua/Dong Fang Hong Satelliten GmbH",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:QueqiaoDFH.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 16.167,
          "end": 23.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.374,
      "end": 30.119,
      "text": "On January 3, 2019, China's Chang'e 4 achieved the first soft landing on the far side.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "ChangE-4 - PCAM.png",
        "credit": "CSNA/Siyu Zhang/Kevin M. Gill",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ChangE-4_-_PCAM.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.367,
          "end": 27.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 27.533,
          "end": 30.133,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.119,
      "end": 37.689,
      "text": "Sunlight sweeps across the entire lunar surface in a repeating cycle of approximately 29.5 days.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "37. Production of phases of the moon (22126908233).jpg",
        "credit": "Community Archives",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:37._Production_of_phases_of_the_moon_(22126908233).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.133,
          "end": 37.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 37.689,
      "end": 42.764,
      "text": "During a new Moon, the far side is actually bathed in blazing daylight.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Tsiolkovskiy Central Peak Oblique (LROC447 - M198059280LR thumb).png",
        "credit": "NASA/GSFC/Arizona State University",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tsiolkovskiy_Central_Peak_Oblique_(LROC447_-_M198059280LR_thumb).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 37.7,
          "end": 42.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 42.764,
      "end": 48.466,
      "text": "Both sides share equal sun, proving that no side is permanently frozen in total darkness.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Tsiolkovskiy crater Apollo 15.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tsiolkovskiy_crater_Apollo_15.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 42.767,
          "end": 48.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
